   "plaque": "arts_branwen",
   "theme": "arts",
   "title": "Branwen ferch Ll\u0177r",
   "text": "The second of the Four Branches of the Mabinogi opens here: Bendigeidfran, giant king of the Island of the Mighty, holds court at Harlech and gives his sister Branwen in marriage to the king of Ireland. Ill-used there, she trains a starling to carry a letter home, and her brother wades the sea to fetch her. The tales survive in manuscripts of the 1300s and 1400s and became the Mabinogion in Lady Charlotte Guest's translation, finished in 1849. The starling is the first messenger in Welsh literature, and it was not paid."
  }
